From: godotjs
Subject: [godotjs] libffi: put win64_armasm.obj where the binaries that need it link it

Windows/arm64 builds libffi's assembly by assembling src/aarch64/win64_armasm.S into a
standalone object and naming that object in the libffi target's own `libraries`. libffi
is a static library, so nothing ever links it and the entry is never used: the three
symbols the object exports - ffi_call_SYSV, ffi_closure_SYSV, ffi_closure_SYSV_V, all
called from src/aarch64/ffi.c - stay undefined, and the first binary to link libffi.lib
stops at its link step (node_mksnapshot.exe: error LNK2019 three times, then LNK1120).
Every other platform gets those symbols inside the archive, because there sysv.S is one
of libffi's sources.

Move the object to the generated-sources directory and repeat the entry under
link_settings, the block gyp merges into the link line of every dependent - the same
route deps/crates/crates.gyp already uses to reach those binaries.

The directory is the part that took a second run to get right. A path arriving through
link_settings is expanded with the depending target's variables, and INTERMEDIATE_DIR
is filled in per target, so naming it there asked link.exe for
obj\node_mksnapshot.gen\win64_armasm.obj - a file that never exists. The ninja
generator defines SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR as PRODUCT_DIR/gen for the whole build
(tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/generator/ninja.py), which is one directory every target agrees
on: the action writes there, libffi names it there, dependents get it from there.
Windows/arm64 only, and the object is still named where it was, so nothing that saw it
before stops seeing it.
diff --git a/deps/libffi/libffi.gyp b/deps/libffi/libffi.gyp
index f3122a4..251ccf7 100644
--- a/deps/libffi/libffi.gyp
+++ b/deps/libffi/libffi.gyp
@@ -311,8 +311,26 @@
         ['OS == "win" and target_arch == "arm64"', {
           # Link the prebuilt object file directly
           'libraries': [
-            '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/win64_armasm.obj',
+            '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/libffi/win64_armasm.obj',
           ],
+          # The block above only reaches a link of libffi itself, and a static library
+          # is never linked, so dependents stopped with unresolved ffi_call_SYSV /
+          # ffi_closure_SYSV / ffi_closure_SYSV_V - the three entry points this object
+          # exports. link_settings is the block gyp merges into the link line of every
+          # dependent.
+          #
+          # The path has to be one every target agrees on, because a path that arrives
+          # through link_settings is expanded with the depending target's variables:
+          # INTERMEDIATE_DIR is filled in per target (asking for
+          # obj/node_mksnapshot.gen/win64_armasm.obj, which never exists), while the
+          # ninja generator defines SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR as PRODUCT_DIR/gen for the
+          # whole build (tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/generator/ninja.py). The action writes
+          # there, libffi names it there, dependents get it from there.
+          'link_settings': {
+            'libraries': [
+              '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/libffi/win64_armasm.obj',
+            ],
+          },
           'actions': [
             {
               'action_name': 'assemble_win64_arm_asm',
@@ -326,7 +344,7 @@
                 '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/libffi/fficonfig.h',
               ],
               'outputs': [
-                '<(INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/win64_armasm.obj',
+                '<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/libffi/win64_armasm.obj',
               ],
               'action': [
                 '<(python)',
